// A numeric literal the lexer can only match part of is refused where it is
// written.
//
// The number pattern accepts `_` between digits but never at an edge, and a
// base prefix must be followed by digits of that base. Without an explicit
// check the leftover characters would lex as an identifier -- `0xZZ` as `0`
// and `ZZ` -- and the program would be rejected somewhere later with a message
// about a stray token instead of about the literal.
//
// Compiled for the diagnostic, so the file never runs.

int32 main() {
    int32 wrong = 0xZZ;
    return wrong;
}
